  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policy-makers network for health policy and systems research</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Convene and facilitate a network of Low- and Middle-Income Country (LMIC) policy-makers to enhance cross-country dialogue, learning and exchange. 
2) Expose policy-makers to innovative approaches in the use of research to improve health and health equity through policy and implementation. 
3) Solicit policy-maker input into the prioritization and execution of health policy and systems research supported by the WHO Alliance.
4) Document lessons learned about working with national leaders to strengthen country capacities for health policy and systems research.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A collaboration between the World Health Organization (WHO) Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research (AHPSR) and the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) to support establishment of a WHO Alliance policy-maker network. This programme of work will: 
- Convene senior policy-makers from Low- and Middle Income Countries (LMICs) for six convenings over a three year period (twice per year). These two-day convenings will take place either in Geneva or in countries where the Alliance is supporting activities; 
- Consult with the network to develop WHO Alliance research priorities; and
- Include the network in ongoing WHO Alliance project policy processes, as a way to socialize emerging research findings.</narrative>
  </description>
